.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 431 AM PDT Tue Aug 25 2026

A robust marine layer was measured at ~1800ft with the KOAK 12z
balloon with primarily IFR/LIFR conditions with the exception of
KAPC, KSJC and KLVK. Mid/high level cloud cover likely helping to
keep the latter three terminals in MVFR/VFR through mid-morning.
Majority of terminals are expected to lift to VFR by late morning,
with KMRY having a 30% chance of lingering past Noon PDT.

Vicinity of SFO...Should remain IFR through mid/late morning
before lifting to VFR for the remainder of the day and evening
hours. KOAK may see MVFR/IFR ceilings return soon after sunset
with KSFO more likely around midnight.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to KOAK with timing of ceilings.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Marine layer is not as deep this far
south, however LIFR ceilings are expected to persist through late
morning, clearing out of KSNS first with KMRY possibly lingering
into early afternoon with VFR until late afternoon early evening.
IFR/LIFR conditions expected from that point on for the remainder
of the forecast period.

